==Maltese==
{{mt-root|r-s-l}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|mt|ar|رَسُول}}. Called an “arabism” by Falzon, but this may mean merely that the word was already highly archaic in the mid-19th century. At any rate it was inherited, not introduced later by Muslim captives, because old sources show that the place {{m|mt||Għajn Rasul}} was always understood as “Spring of the Apostle [Paul]”.

